## Why This Is Asked

Tests depth of cross-DC security, dynamic policy loading, and automated risk controls in a real-world Docker DC architecture.

## Key Concepts

- SPIFFE/SVIDs with Vault
- WASM-based per-tenant policy engine
- Edge verifier sidecar for SVID validation
- Canary deployments and automatic rollback
- Cross-DC routing and observability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: load tenant policy from broker and validate SVID before calling app
async function handleRequest(req){
  const svid = await verifySVID(req.headers['spiffe']);
  const(policy) = await loadPolicyFromBroker(req.tenant);
  if(!policy.allows(req)) throw new Error('Access denied');
  return proxyToApp(req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you debug a scenario where Vault rotation invalidates existing SVIDs mid-rollout?
- What metrics and traces would you collect to enforce the 25% canary SLA thresholds across DCs?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to add a real, cross-DC capability using Docker Configs, a TLS edge (Traefik), and a simple stateful component (Redis). It also touches observability (metrics) and inter-DC consistency via pub/sub.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant rate limiting with Redis counters
- Docker Configs for per-tenant quotas
- Cross-DC synchronization via Redis Pub/Sub
- TLS termination with Traefik edge proxy
- Metrics exposure for Prometheus

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-rate-limit middleware sketch
const quota = getQuotaFromConfig(req.headers['X-Tenant']);
const key = `rl:${tenant}:${windowStart}`;
let count = redis.incr(key);
if (count === 1) redis.expire(key, windowSeconds);
if (count > quota) {
  res.status(429).set('Retry-After', String(windowSeconds)).send('Too Many Requests');
} else {
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test burst traffic and quota drift across DCs?
- What strategies ensure accurate time windows across replicas?
- How would you monitor per-tenant usage and alert on anomalies?
